# Test email addresses

Never ask me to create a new mailbox, email account, address or alias for a test, a drill or a throwaway user. Use plus-addressing of my own address:
{{ $bases := get . "plusAddressBases" -}}
{{ if $bases -}}
{{ range splitList "," $bases }}{{ $parts := splitList "@" (trim .) }}
- `{{ index $parts 0 }}+<purpose>@{{ index $parts 1 }}`
{{- end }}
{{- else }}
- This machine has no `plusAddressBases` in its chezmoi data. Ask me for my address.
{{- end }}

If a service refuses a `+` address, stop and ask me. Never fall back to a new address.

Why: a new mailbox or alias is costly to create and to delete, and the number I can hold is limited. A mailbox that still holds mail cannot be deleted cleanly.
